    "rich_text_intro": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "text_intro": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>This is a salad with no lettuce in it. Smashed Persian cucumbers, ripe summer peaches, avocado and a fistful of cilantro, with seared Black Tiger Shrimp on top and one big drizzle of ginger ponzu over the whole thing. Roughly twenty minutes, and the only thing that touches heat is the shrimp.</p><p>The shrimp cook in about four minutes total &mdash; one to two minutes a side in a hot cast iron pan, seasoned with nothing but salt, pepper and grated garlic. You are looking for bright orange with slightly crisp edges, then straight out of the pan while you build the bowl.</p><p>We made it with Seatopia <a href=\"/products/black-tiger-shrimp-mangrove-regeneration\" title=\"Mangrove Black Tiger Shrimp\">Mangrove Black Tiger Shrimp</a> from Tarakan, Indonesia &mdash; raw, easy-peel, head-off, and lab tested to the <a href=\"/pages/why-clean-seafood-matters\" title=\"Why Clean Seafood Matters\">Seatopia Standard&trade;</a>. The dressing is Ginger Ponzu from <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/eat___sunny/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"Sunny Fine Foods on Instagram\">Sunny Fine Foods</a>, the Los Angeles brand Matt and Nora Kramer built around dressings with nothing hiding in them &mdash; no gums, no fillers, no blanket &ldquo;natural flavors.&rdquo; Same instinct we have about fish.</p>",
            "text_size": "subtext-md",
            "text_max_size": 32,
            "text_font": "body",
            "secondary_color": false,
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_intro"
      ],
