      "blocks": {
        "p_shrimp": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "lightning",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "1. Seared shrimp",
            "text": "<p>Salt, pepper, grated garlic, hot cast iron. Black Tiger Shrimp hold their snap instead of going rubbery, which is the whole reason they work cold in a salad.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "p_cuke": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "organic",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "2. Smashed cucumber",
            "text": "<p>Smashed rather than sliced, so the ragged edges catch dressing. Persian cucumbers have thin skins and almost no seeds, so there is nothing to peel or scoop.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "p_fruit": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "star",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "3. Peach and avocado",
            "text": "<p>The peach brings acid and perfume, the avocado brings fat. Together they do the job a creamy dressing would normally have to do.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "p_dressing": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "box",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "4. Ginger ponzu",
            "text": "<p>Citrus, soy and fresh ginger, never heat pasteurized and with no added sugar. It goes on at the very end, straight from the bottle, in one generous pass.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
